Jaybay (widely known online as Jaybay Animal, 6ix Animal, or Jay the Animal) is an independent Brooklyn-based underground rapper who gained viral traction in New York City's hip-hop and drill scene. [1, 2, 3]

Artist Profile & Details
Real Name. His birth name has not been publicly disclosed, as he operates strictly under his stage aliases. (Note: Some social media blogs have confused him with Queens rapper Bay Swag, whose birth name is Lloyd McKenzie Jr., though they are separate artists.) [1, 2, 3]
Rap Type & Style. He performs New York drill and underground hip-hop. His style is defined by raw, high-energy freestyles, an intense physical delivery, and aggressive street-oriented bars. Notable tracks include "Shell After Shell," "20 Large," "To The Left," and his 2026 EP Public Defender. [1, 2, 3]
Record Label Deal. He is currently unsigned / independent. He went viral after publicly demanding a $20 million record deal from major labels—specifically calling out Sony, Republic, and EMPIRE—and reportedly walking out of label meetings after his asking price was declined. [1, 2, 3]
Home Address. Specific residential addresses are private and not publicly available. He is publicly associated with Brooklyn, New York, specifically referencing Flatbush and filming street performances in Brownsville. [1, 2]
Business & Management Info. He does not have a public corporate office address listed, though his music is represented through independent management teams listed on his official @jaybayanimal Instagram (@touchamilldaexecutive and @moreno_from_brooklyn). [1]


